Backport of upstream google/or-tools commit 741965107 ("util: fix python
wrappers build", 2026-03-19, after v9.15), taken from
https://github.com/google/or-tools/commit/741965107.patch. The commit edits
ortools/util/python/wrappers.cc, where upstream later moved the generator; at
v9.15 the file is ortools/sat/python/wrappers.cc, so the paths below are
retargeted and the hunks apply unchanged.

The generator writes the pybind11 wrappers of SatParameters from string
templates. pybind11 3 rejects extra call policies in the def_property family
("def_property family does not currently support keep_alive"), and the two
def_property_readonly templates for repeated fields passed
py::keep_alive<0, 1>(). return_value_policy::reference_internal ties the
returned reference to the owner object instead. The .def templates keep their
keep_alive, which .def accepts.

From 741965107e93aca455e84c349edafc7f914debdd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Corentin Le Molgat <corentinl@google.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Mar 2026 10:22:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] util: fix python wrappers build

---
 ortools/sat/python/wrappers.cc | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ortools/sat/python/wrappers.cc b/ortools/sat/python/wrappers.cc

--- a/ortools/sat/python/wrappers.cc
+++ b/ortools/sat/python/wrappers.cc
@@ -370,7 +370,7 @@ class Generator {
     .def_property_readonly(
         "$0",
         []($1 self) { return self->mutable_$2(); },
-        py::return_value_policy::reference, py::keep_alive<0, 1>()))",
+        py::return_value_policy::reference_internal))",
           field.name(), current_context_.self_mutable_name, field.name());
       // We'll need to generate the wrapping for
       // `google::protobuf::RepeatedPtrField<$3>`.
@@ -383,7 +383,7 @@ class Generator {
     .def_property_readonly(
         "$0",
         []($1 self) { return self->mutable_$0(); },
-        py::return_value_policy::reference, py::keep_alive<0, 1>()))",
+        py::return_value_policy::reference_internal))",
                                 field.name(),
                                 current_context_.self_mutable_name);
       // We'll need to generate the wrapping for
